        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-24T13:16:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So some caller above this code is going to have to do a check whether a proxy is volatile or not so that it can be placed in the volatile set on the Recording. So it seems like that same logic can restrict only calling this on non-volatile proxies.\n\nIt just seems weird to me as a caller that i could do\nproxy-\u003einstantiate(); // returns true since volatile\nproxy-\u003eisInstantiated(); //returns false\n\nIf we don\u0027t want to add logic to enforce calling this on non-volatile proxies only, maybe we could have the return be a tri-state enum instead of a bool. FailedInstantiationg, SkippedForVolatile, Instantiated.",
      "parentUuid": "a5b17ec9_4933d0c4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 67,
        "endChar": 23
      },
